1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:03,210
In 1944, two French cyclists watched four

2
00:00:03,210 --> 00:00:05,400
American soldiers pick up a Sherman tank.

3
00:00:05,638 --> 00:00:07,958
One soldier reportedly shrugged: "Americans

4
00:00:07,958 --> 00:00:08,948
are very strong."

5
00:00:09,275 --> 00:00:10,305
The tank was a balloon.

6
00:00:10,675 --> 00:00:11,925
It weighed 93 pounds.

7
00:00:12,347 --> 00:00:15,127
It belonged to the Ghost Army: 1,100 Americans

8
00:00:15,127 --> 00:00:17,673
whose job was to look like 30,000.

9
00:00:17,683 --> 00:00:19,783
Many were artists, recruited from art schools

10
00:00:19,783 --> 00:00:20,793
and ad agencies.

11
00:00:21,126 --> 00:00:22,336
They inflated fake tanks,

12
00:00:22,566 --> 00:00:24,076
trucks and cannons in a few hours.

13
00:00:24,312 --> 00:00:26,232
Sound trucks blasted recordings of tank

14
00:00:26,232 --> 00:00:28,182
columns that carried 15 miles.

15
00:00:29,012 --> 00:00:30,692
Radio operators faked the chatter of entire

16
00:00:30,692 --> 00:00:31,422
divisions.

17
00:00:31,813 --> 00:00:33,143
From Normandy to the Rhine,

18
00:00:33,233 --> 00:00:34,843
they staged more than twenty deceptions.

19
00:00:35,195 --> 00:00:37,225
The biggest came in March 1945.

20
00:00:38,295 --> 00:00:39,875
Along the Rhine, they set up more than 600

21
00:00:39,875 --> 00:00:42,185
dummies and impersonated two divisions.

22
00:00:42,590 --> 00:00:43,690
The Germans took the bait.

23
00:00:43,690 --> 00:00:45,970
To the north, the real Ninth Army crossed

24
00:00:45,970 --> 00:00:47,680
the river and met little resistance.

25
00:00:48,250 --> 00:00:50,580
The unit stayed secret until 1996.

26
00:00:51,450 --> 00:00:53,650
In 2022, they were awarded the Congressional

27
00:00:53,650 --> 00:00:54,520
Gold Medal.

28
00:00:54,846 --> 00:00:55,846
An army of artists,

29
00:00:55,846 --> 00:00:57,926
fighting with balloons. Would you have fallen

30
00:00:57,926 --> 00:00:58,516
for it?

